== 1. the rule against the table ==
every sequence of the other side's moves up to 12 rounds: the table and the rule in words disagree in 0 cases

== 2. the three games of the picture (14 rounds, as handshake_strip_phone.py) ==
two of the machines, slip by the first in round 8    DDCCCCCDCDDCCC | DDCCCCCCDDDCCC   points (33, 33)
machine / always cooperates                          DDDDDDDDDDDDDD | CCCCCCCCCCCCCC   points (70, 0)
machine / always defects                             DDCDDCDDCDDCDD | DDDDDDDDDDDDDD   points (10, 30)
older machine / always defects                       DCDCDCDCDCDCDC | DDDDDDDDDDDDDD   points (7, 42)
third game: rounds in which the machine cooperates: [3, 6, 9, 12]
first game: rounds after the slip in which both cooperate again from: 12

== 3. what a round is worth with no slips (long run, exact fractions over a whole cycle) ==
always-defects against the machine                                 first player   7/3 = 2.333 a round; second player   2/3 = 0.667
machine against machine                                            first player     3 = 3.000 a round; second player     3 = 3.000
always-defects against always-defects                              first player     1 = 1.000 a round; second player     1 = 1.000
always-defects against the one-defection machine                   first player     3 = 3.000 a round; second player   1/2 = 0.500
always-cooperates against the machine                              first player     0 = 0.000 a round; second player     5 = 5.000
always-defects against the machine begun at its 2nd state          first player   7/3 = 2.333 a round; second player   2/3 = 0.667
always-defects against the machine begun at its cooperating state  first player   7/3 = 2.333 a round; second player   2/3 = 0.667

